Only the `focal` line moves, and it moves to nothing: centring within
cue deletes the between-cue main effect by construction. Every test the
thesis actually interprets -- x, focal:x, and the three-way term -- is
unchanged. Had the ANOVA been run on y_i_mc, the conclusions would have
been the same, minus one effect that would have been structurally zero.


=== 4. WHAT THE CENTRED SCALE COSTS THE READER ===

Figure 3.1 plots the centred outcome for each cue in the same panel. Since
each cue was shifted by its own constant, the vertical position of a line
is not a level of intention to download: it is a level relative to that
cue's own average. Ordering of the lines is therefore not interpretable,
while their slopes are.

